<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore weekly oil product stocks up.</title>
<headline>Singapore weekly oil product stocks up.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore weekly residue stocks rose by 519,000 barrels in the week ended September 25 to 9.737 million barrels, Singapore's Trade Development Board (TDB) said.</p>
<p>They include HSFO, LSFO, LSWR and the straight-run atmospheric residue, but exclude bitumen.</p>
<p>Middle-distillate stocks jumped 879,000 barrels to 8.415 million barrels.</p>
<p>Middle distillates comprise jet, kerosene and gas oil.</p>
<p>Light distillate stocks similarly rose by 583,00 barrels to 6.084 million barrels. They comprise gasoline, reformate and naphtha. -- Singapore newsroom (65-870-3082)</p>
</text>
